    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Initial Access (legitimate)", "technique": "T1078.002", "what_happened": "After-hours AzureAD sign-in for hr.manager@company.com at 2026-04-11 21:40:08 MYT. MFA satisfied (1 push), Device=registered (HR-LAP-011), Location=Malaysia. The login itself is technically authorised — hr.manager is a real account with valid credentials and proper MFA. The anomaly is TIME: this user's historical baseline is 09:00-18:00 MYT, and they have NEVER signed in after 19:30 MYT in the last 90 days.", "chain_reason": "AzureAD audit (Wazuh azure-logs module, rule 91540): data.azure.identity=hr.manager@company.com, data.azure.appDisplayName=Microsoft 365, data.azure.deviceDetail=HR-LAP-011, data.azure.location=Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia, data.azure.mfaDetail.attempts=1. Conditional Access did not fire because all individual checks pass (device compliant, MFA satisfied, country whitelisted). This is the canonical 'insider with valid credentials' problem.", "first_seen": "2026-04-11T21:40:08+0800"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Collection (bulk sensitive access)", "technique": "T1213", "what_happened": "Within 60 seconds of login, hr.manager accessed sensitive SharePoint folders that they typically touch only during quarterly cycles: /HR/Payroll/Payroll_All.xlsx, /HR/Disciplinary/2024_2025.docx, /HR/Termination/Exit_List.pdf. No business process correlates with this access (no payroll cycle, no audit, no scheduled review).", "chain_reason": "M365 audit log (rule 91610): data.azure.identity=hr.manager@company.com, data.azure.operation=FileAccessed, file paths under /HR/Payroll/, /HR/Disciplinary/, /HR/Termination/. Baseline shows hr.manager touches Payroll_All.xlsx ~4 times/year (quarterly). Tonight: 3 files in 3 distinct sensitive categories within 90 seconds = systematic harvest.", "first_seen": "2026-04-11T21:41:33+0800"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Collection / Staging", "technique": "T1074.001", "what_happened": "At 21:44:12, a new folder C:\\Users\\hr.manager\\Documents\\backup_staging\\ was created on HR-LAP-011, and the 3 SharePoint files were copied locally (via OneDrive Sync, then user-initiated copy).", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 11 batch (rule 61603): targetFilename matches C:\\Users\\hr.manager\\Documents\\backup_staging\\Payroll_All.xlsx, Disciplinary_2024_2025.docx, Exit_List.pdf — all created within 8 seconds, by image=explorer.exe under user=CORP\\hr.manager. Local staging step before bulk upload.", "first_seen": "2026-04-11T21:44:12+0800"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Execution (legitimate tool, abnormal trigger)", "technique": "T1059", "what_happened": "At 21:46:12, BackupSync.exe version 4.2.1 (a corporately-approved sync utility) was launched MANUALLY on HR-LAP-011 by hr.manager. Normal use of this tool in the org is via the scheduled task 'BackupSync-Nightly' triggered at 23:30 by SYSTEM context. Manual launch by an end-user is unusual but allowed.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon Event 1 (rule 92010): image=C:\\Program Files\\BackupSync\\BackupSync.exe, parentImage=C:\\Windows\\explorer.exe (interactive user launch), user=CORP\\hr.manager, commandLine includes --target=cloud-sync-storage.com/hr-manager-personal --source=C:\\Users\\hr.manager\\Documents\\backup_staging\\. Target is a PERSONAL cloud-sync-storage.com bucket — not the corporate sync tenant (corporate sync target is corp-backup.company.com per HR-LAP-011's scheduled task config).", "first_seen": "2026-04-11T21:46:12+0800"},
